    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/6/46409.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 14,
    "turn_text": "You know, when I first saw what was going on, I immediately resisted as an individualist and a libertarian, all the stuff that were telling me what to do and questioned the science of wearing masks, shutting schools down, all that. From the very beginning, I questioned that. But on the origins of the virus, whether it came from a lab or not, I do remember reading Nicholas Wade's article. And he had been, I think, a New York Times science writer. He's written books. He understands the science that can explain it in a real way. And he wrote something on medium.com. And I didn't know much about that. I think it's a self-publishing. And then the story was told that most of the major outlets wouldn't take it. He's an esteemed writer, a good writer. And he explained science in such a way that the ordinary person could it. could understand it, and what he explained was that a virus can actually be mutated, pushed through natural selection evolution in a petri dish, and it actually turns out when you look at it, you cannot see that the sciences have manipulated. It's forced evolution. It's just passing it over and over again, and basically what they do is they take an animal like a mouse, and they put a human lungs in it. Now, that's another story in and of itself, but they humanize the lungs. The immune system thinks it's seeing a human lung instead of a mouse. Cell markers are human, and this is done genetically through manipulation. But then what they do is run the virus through there. The first time the virus says, well, those are humans, it doesn't work very well. They do it again and again until they get lucky and the virus mutates and it infects one of these humanized mice. But then they let it grow, they take it out again and then they do it again. It's called serial passage. You keep infecting the mice. What you get is forcing evolution. What might happen in nature to go from animals to human is now being done by humans forcing an animal virus to become a human virus. And it has sort of scary implications. Because what ended up happening, and then there's another good book called Viral, and in that Alina Chan and Matt Ridley write about this, and they say that basically the virus appeared to be pre-adapted for human, just ready to take off. And so when I read Nicholas Wade's article, I became fascinated by this. and sort of got into it because it truly is a mystery with all of these clues. of them are 100% certain. They're circumstantial, but so many clues, one after another. But then the real hook for me was that I was, as I was learning of the facts of that this virus had been manipulated, was that all of a sudden Every all of the people that doubted this were being called crazy, conspiracy theorists, loony, by scientists, by Anthony Fauci and by all his cronies. But then we discover about a year into the research that was going on with this, we discover all these people were privately saying the opposite. In fact, even using the same words, this is not fringe theory. Christian Andersen, one of the main scientists who writes the paper to say, Oh, this is crazy. All the people saying it's crazy publicly in private Senate. Yeah, I'm pretty sure, you know, for sure. This cake looks manipulated here to me. And we know they're doing gain of function research in move on all the stuff that they're publicly denying to me. To me, it's the One cover up from government that's so thoroughly debunked by its own people.",
