    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/6/46409.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 30,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, and I've introduced it. What we would do is take Dr. Fauci's position and divide it into three. So it'd be three different people. So there'd be a third as much power, but then we have term limits. I think it's two, five year terms, and we make it confirmable by the Senate. Right now the Senate doesn't vote on Fauci's position. And it's one person who can do it for 45 years. The closest analogy to the abuse of power, and it probably pales in comparison would be Jaguar. Jaguar did a lot of bad things over 40 years and accumulated a lot.",
