    "turn_idx": 41,
    "turn_text": "And there's a lot of national defense stuff going on at this. And then there's a huge amount of money. I mean, let's say that it's a noble thing to protect our soldiers against anthrax and we eat a vaccine. Vaccine, I think, goes bad in about a year or two. And then we do it again just to the tune of millions and millions of dollars. And I'm not making a conclusion on whether we need that or not. Maybe we do. But at the same time, there are billions of dollars changing hands in this. And there needs to be oversight. So one of our goals for oversight of this is that the people funding the agencies should not be the people receiving the month. So the people overseeing the these potential.",
