  {
    "episode_id": 46409,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/6/46409.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 58,
    "turn_text": "But you think about it. Science is really a field of disputation. Einstein said, I'm always one experiment away from being disproven. And I realized that I have to keep backing up what I say. And I have to hope the experiments come by support me because I'm one way. And if you've ever been to a scientific convention, they're always going back and forth saying, we didn't like you study size. We didn't like the grouping was in good control group. This disputation goes on all the time. Whenever someone talks about scientific consensus, consensus only happens when you centralize the funding of science. So really, the precursor to what we've gotten here with the misinformation and the unification of one government think on this was climate change. All of the climate research in the whole world is funded by government. All the conclusions are predesited. There is no objective climate science. I know that sounds like a lot, but I don't believe there's any objective science funded by government because if you are a skeptic or have a real question, you want to know, is this true? You will not be published. But it's the same with COVID thing. So with COVID thing, there was only one truth and the one truth is take the vaccine shut up and take the vaccine. And they were unwilling and really want you challenge them unwilling and unable to answer the questions or the challenge.",
