    "turn_text": "You know, I think they continue to try, but it's lost its potency, both literally and figuratively, because frankly, people say, oh, gosh, I'm so glad I had six vaccines that didn't die from my latest bout with COVID. But I think people are smarter than that. And they're starting to know that basically the disease itself has become less potent. And this is not always true, but it is often true that viruses that last for a while and humanity survives become less potent over time and sometimes more contagious. So like with Omicron, it became so contagious that everybody, the whole world was inoculated, but fortunately it was less potent. Now some, there's a couple arguments. You can say less people died because they already had a vaccine maybe. And some of it already had the first, the wild type variant like I had in the very beginning. So that made it less potent. But also I think the virus is less potent now. And so I don't know if we can still be a weapon. I don't know. I'm going to the airport now. I go to the airport twice a week. And for the last year, it's probably been 5% of the people with masks. It's 10% or 15% of the people with masks again. And it's completely irrational, one because the disease is in codes not dangerous anymore. You've either added or been vaccinated or both. And frankly, the masks don't work. So you're not going to die from it. And the masks don't work. And you used to have people have been called into this. I've been just sort of And I guess it was that way in Asia, you know, if you've been wearing masks and someone just never gave up on wearing masks, it's to me sort of a sad sort of statement. And I can't imagine growing up as a kid in Texas wearing a mask outside, you know, playing ball in a mask.",
