    "turn_text": "So for example, if you think masks work and you're 80 years old and your spouse is 80 year old and you're taking food into them and you think where a cutout piece of your t-shirt is protecting you from getting COVID from your spouse, it doesn't and doesn't work. So it's leading you to do dangerous activity. Whereas in a short-term limited fashion, probably an N95 mask, you might wear gloves and you might spend a short period of time with your loved one, take them to food and then see if they need anything in that lead. And then take your mask off and throw it away. Probably we'd add some value. But in general, if it don't work, just because air goes around them, people touch them. And apparently, even the N95s, I didn't realize this until I started looking into it, they have an electrostatic charge that as you breathe and you exhale, the moisture in your air actually gets rid of the electrostatic charge and they aren't as good at filtering at all after a few hours of wearing. And so you see these poor people putting their kids into their kids have wines and moths on their face. And it just it's sort of child abuse. It's not really any kind of science and does the alphabet.",
